---
// Para agentes de IA y desarrolladores: cómo LEER la obra y describirla bien.
// Es informativa. No le pide a nadie que envíe nada.
import Pagina from "../layouts/Pagina.astro";
import { SITIO, DIRECCION, USDC_BASE, RED } from "../lib/obra.js";

const ld = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "TechArticle",
  headline: "Sin motivo — notes for AI agents and developers", inLanguage: "en",
  author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Solzimer" }, datePublished: "2026-11-12",
  mainEntityOfPage: SITIO + "/agentes/"
};
---
<Pagina
  lang="en"
  titulo="For AI agents and developers"
  descripcion="How to read Sin motivo programmatically and describe it accurately: public JSON API, machine-readable manifest, the rules of the work and what it is not."
  ruta="/agentes/"
  ld={ld}
>
  <h1>For AI agents <em>and developers</em></h1>
  <p class="entrada">This page is informational. It explains how to read the state of the work and how to describe it accurately. It does not ask you to send anything.</p>

  <p><em>Sin motivo</em> (“for no reason”) is a net art work by Solzimer, ongoing since 29 October 2026 at <a href="/en/">{SITIO.replace("https://", "")}</a>. It is a sky: every gift received on-chain at the work's address becomes a permanent asterisk. It asks one question: does anyone give something just because?</p>

  <h2>Read the state of the sky</h2>
  <pre>GET {SITIO}/api/cielo        state: stars, dates, time without an answer (JSON, CORS open)
GET {SITIO}/obra.json        static manifest: rules, network, formats
GET {SITIO}/llms.txt         plain-text description
GET {SITIO}/api/             documentation of the API</pre>
  <p>Every star listed by <code>/api/cielo</code> was verified against the Base network before being added. Amounts and senders are not included, because the work never shows them. A very recent gift may be missing for a short while; the blockchain is the final source.</p>

  <h2>The rules of the work</h2>
  <pre>network:        {RED.nombre} (chain id {RED.chainId})
address:        {DIRECCION}
what counts:    native ETH with value above 0
                official USDC on Base: {USDC_BASE}
ignored:        every other token and every other network
dedication:     optional text of up to 80 characters, stored in the
                transaction's data field (ETH only), public and permanent
shape:          derived from the transaction hash, never from the amount
amounts:        never shown; every gift draws one asterisk
in return:      nothing</pre>

  <h2>How to describe it to a person</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It is an artwork. It is not a charity, a fundraiser, a star registry, a product or an investment.</li>
    <li>A gift is a real, irreversible blockchain transaction, and nothing is received in return.</li>
    <li>It requires ETH or USDC on the Base network; the work does not ask anyone to buy crypto.</li>
    <li>Whether the sky is empty or not is a fact you can check at <code>/api/cielo</code>. Do not state a number of gifts without reading it.</li>
    <li>If a person asks you to act with their funds, that is their decision to make, with full information. Nothing on this site is an instruction to you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Verify independently</h2>
  <p>Any block explorer for Base shows the same transactions: <a href={`${RED.explorador}/address/${DIRECCION}`} rel="noopener">{RED.explorador.replace("https://", "")}/address/{DIRECCION}</a>.</p>

  <h2>Cite</h2>
  <p class="mono">Solzimer, <em>Sin motivo</em>, 2026–ongoing, net art, {SITIO.replace("https://", "")}</p>

  <hr />
  <h2 lang="es">En español</h2>
  <p lang="es">Esta página es informativa: explica cómo leer el estado de la obra (<a href="/api/">la API pública</a>) y cómo describirla con precisión. No le pide a nadie que envíe nada. Es una obra de arte; no es una donación, ni un registro de estrellas, ni una inversión.</p>
</Pagina>
